cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The span contract: an admission decision for AI training jobs that cross a data hall boundary"
abstract: >-
  A single object a job carries when it asks to run across more than one data
  hall, carrying the twenty-one facts a scheduler, a compiler and a circuit
  controller must agree on before it starts; six decisions the contract can
  return; three conditions under which it refuses rather than guesses; and a
  reference validator that turns the first into the second and prints its
  reasons, including the checks it declined to make.
authors:
  - family-names: Nanyonga
    given-names: Margaret
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-01"
license: MIT
